<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>Hands the downloaded GIMP installer (an EXE) to the package tool (pcman), which publishes it as a new version of the template item into the Cimian repository, or says that nothing is new. For an EXE the package tool is given the version label: the recipe passes the GIMP version that the download recipe's GimpInfoProvider read from the installer's file name (three numbers, such as 3.2.8), never the installer's revision, so a re-issued installer of a version that the repository has is "nothing new". Whether the file has a version resource, and what the installed program reports, is NOT established: the first dry run shows the label. The download's SHA-256 comes from a mirror (see the download recipe): the shared importer counts it as verified, but it is a transfer check, not proof of origin. This recipe was NOT run with AutoPkg. This is a dry run, which writes nothing, until the recipe's override sets pcman_dry_run to false.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.pcman.GIMP</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>GIMP</string>
            <key>PCMAN_TEMPLATE</key>
            <string>gimp</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>ParentRecipe</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.GIMP-Win</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.PcmanProcessors/PcmanImporter</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>pcman_template</key>
                    <string>%PCMAN_TEMPLATE%</string>
                    <key>pcman_version</key>
                    <string>%version%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
